.TH GKNOWLEDGE 1 "October 2026" "gknowledge 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gknowledge \- native GNOME app that turns documents into a cited wiki
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gknowledge
[\fIGTK-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gknowledge
collects documents, notes and links and turns them into a linked
Markdown wiki in which every page records its sources. Questions are
answered from the wiki with numbered citations.
.PP
A project is a plain folder of Markdown files with wikilinks and front
matter, plus an SQLite index. It can be opened in other Markdown editors
or kept under version control.
.PP
The app works offline with a built-in engine. A model provider (Ollama,
LM Studio, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a ChatGPT plan) can be
chosen in Preferences.
.SH OPTIONS
Standard GTK and GApplication options are accepted, for example
.BR \-\-help .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gknowledge/
Recent projects and provider settings (defaults to
.IR ~/.config/gknowledge/ ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gknowledge\-mcp (1)
.PP
https://github.com/openapi/gknowledge
